  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "A researcher and YouTuber named Chris Ramsay, speaking on Jesse Michels' podcast, tells of Stargate, a US government programme that ran from the 1970s to 1995 and studied remote viewing, the claimed ability to describe distant places or things using only the mind. Ramsay says that each year one of its best-known viewers, a man named Joe McMoneagle, would go into a SCIF, a sealed and secure room for handling classified material, and do a remote viewing session so that officials would see results and renew the programme's budget. If true, it would mean the government kept paying for psychic spying because it seemed to work."
